{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-35094","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52755","text":"TRAAVIIS — Split Evaluation Closure ("},{"id":"spn-52756","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-52757","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-35095","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52758","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date"},{"id":"spn-52759","text":" 2026-07-24 · "},{"id":"spn-52760","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status"},{"id":"spn-52761","text":" shipped, 15 new laws green, 314 tests green "},{"id":"spn-52762","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope"},{"id":"spn-52763","text":" RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md §7 — the last unbuilt item in the build order that is not explicitly deferred. "},{"id":"spn-52764","marks":["code"],"text":"serve"},{"id":"spn-52765","text":" (D5) and "},{"id":"spn-52766","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-52767","text":" remain open."}]},{"id":"blk-35096","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52768","text":"1. What shipped"}]},{"id":"blk-35097","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52769","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-52770","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-52771","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-52772","text":" closed authoring. "},{"id":"spn-52773","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-52774","text":" closed one task. The remaining gap was the one §7 names last:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35099","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52775","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-52776","text":" — run an agent over a split, emit an "},{"id":"spn-52777","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-52778","text":" per task, score."}]}],"id":"blk-35098","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-35100","kind":"code","language":"sh","text":"trvs pack lab lab-pkg\ntrvs eval lab-pkg --split test --output episodes/ --agent python3 agent.py\ntrvs verify-episode episodes/episode-cfef6da4…      # replays with no agent"},{"id":"blk-35101","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52779","text":"Verified end to end on a hand-authored three-task environment:"}]},{"id":"blk-35102","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"pack →  env-aa7df5dd…   task-3b4b2599…  task-082e11c1…  task-0cd4992e…\n        closure ✓  reopened ✓\n\neval --split test\n  [1/2] ✓ task-082e11c181f3be21aa82e138  ok  reward 1\n  [2/2] ✓ task-0cd4992e274e07fc7da0bddd  ok  reward 1\n  ok            2/2\n  mean reward   1\n  evaluation    episodes/evaluation.json\n\nverify-episode (each, no agent process) → ✓ closed"},{"id":"blk-35103","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52780","text":"2. The load-bearing decision: "},{"id":"spn-52781","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-52782","text":" mints no identity"}]},{"id":"blk-35104","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52783","text":"§1's ladder ends at "},{"id":"spn-52784","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-52785","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-52786","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-52787","text":". There is "},{"id":"spn-52788","marks":["bold"],"text":"no rung for \"a run over a split\""},{"id":"spn-52789","text":", so this command does not create one. What it returns is an "},{"id":"spn-52790","marks":["italic"],"text":"index"},{"id":"spn-52791","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-35105","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"evaluation_version\": \"traaviis.evaluation.v1\",\n  \"env_id\": \"env-…\", \"split\": \"test\",\n  \"episodes\": [ {\"task_id\": \"task-…\", \"episode_id\": \"episode-…\",\n                 \"status\": \"ok\", \"reward\": 1.0, \"bundle\": \"episode-…\"} ],\n  \"totals\": {\"tasks\": 2, \"ok\": 2, \"reward_mean\": 1.0, …} }"},{"id":"blk-35106","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52792","text":"Every id in it is derived somewhere else. The index itself is not content-addressed and carries no id — a law (E5) scans the emitted JSON and fails on any "},{"id":"spn-52793","marks":["code"],"text":"<prefix>-<hex>"},{"id":"spn-52794","text":" family outside "},{"id":"spn-52795","marks":["code"],"text":"{env, task, episode, snap, sem}"},{"id":"spn-52796","text":", and on any "},{"id":"spn-52797","marks":["code"],"text":"evaluation_id"},{"id":"spn-52798","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-52799","marks":["code"],"text":"run_id"},{"id":"spn-52800","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-52801","marks":["code"],"text":"eval_id"},{"id":"spn-52802","text":" key."}]},{"id":"blk-35107","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52803","text":"This is deliberate restraint, not an oversight. A defensible "},{"id":"spn-52804","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-…"},{"id":"spn-52805","text":" would have to close over "},{"id":"spn-52806","marks":["italic"],"text":"the agent"},{"id":"spn-52807","text":", and there is no agent identity rung — so any id minted today would be under-determined, and a later real one would silently disagree with it. See §6.1."}]},{"id":"blk-35108","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52808","text":"3. Nothing runs until everything checkable has been checked"}]},{"id":"blk-35109","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52809","text":"The order mirrors "},{"id":"spn-52810","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-52811","text":"'s, for the same reason:"}]},{"id":"blk-35110","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"1. open_package     reopen through §5a — env-/task-/rew-/snap- ALL re-derived\n                    from the written bytes\n2. resolve split    the split exists, is non-empty, every member is in-closure\n3. admit subject    bind the on-disk tree to snapshot.json (once, shared)\n--- only now is a process launched ---\n4. per task         evaluate → optionally persist episode-<id>/\n5. aggregate        index written atomically (temp sibling + one rename)"},{"id":"blk-35111","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52812","text":"Two laws prove the boundary is real rather than decorative: E2 tampers a packed task and E2b drifts one subject byte, then passes an agent that writes a marker file. Both refuse with a typed code ("},{"id":"spn-52813","marks":["code"],"text":"REOPEN_TASK_ID"},{"id":"spn-52814","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-52815","marks":["code"],"text":"SUBJECT_*"},{"id":"spn-52816","text":") "},{"id":"spn-52817","marks":["bold"],"text":"and the marker never appears"},{"id":"spn-52818","text":" — a broken package costs zero episodes, not N wasted ones."}]},{"id":"blk-35112","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52819","text":"4. A split is a set — so its order is not observable"}]},{"id":"blk-35113","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52820","text":"§3 says splits are \""},{"id":"spn-52821","marks":["bold"],"text":"named sets"},{"id":"spn-52822","text":" of "},{"id":"spn-52823","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-52824","text":" ids\". Taken literally that has a consequence the previous "},{"id":"spn-52825","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-52826","text":" did not honour: it stored split membership in source order, so listing the same two tasks the other way round produced a different "},{"id":"spn-52827","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-52828","text":". Two identical environments, two identities."}]},{"id":"blk-35114","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52829","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-52830","text":" now canonicalizes a split as a "},{"id":"spn-52831","marks":["bold"],"text":"sorted set"},{"id":"spn-52832","text":", and a repeated member is "},{"id":"spn-52833","marks":["code"],"text":"SPLIT_DUPLICATE"},{"id":"spn-52834","text":" rather than being silently collapsed (pack never repairs a scaffold). "},{"id":"spn-52835","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-52836","text":" then derives its run order as the sorted task ids, so the order tasks execute in is a function of the environment, never of how someone typed the manifest. E1 packs two environments differing only in split order and asserts byte-identical "},{"id":"spn-52837","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-52838","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-35115","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52839","text":"5. Laws (15 new, all green)"}]},{"id":"blk-35116","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52840","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_eval_split.py"},{"id":"spn-52841","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-35117","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35119","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52842","marks":["bold"],"text":"E1"},{"id":"spn-52843","text":" split order does not move "},{"id":"spn-52844","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-52845","text":"; the packed manifest is sorted ·"}]}],"id":"blk-35118","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35120","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52846","text":"duplicate member refused, nothing written."}]},{"id":"blk-35121","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35123","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52847","marks":["bold"],"text":"E2"},{"id":"spn-52848","text":" tampered package and drifted subject both refuse **before any agent"}]}],"id":"blk-35122","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35124","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52849","text":"process starts** (proved with a marker-writing agent)."}]},{"id":"blk-35125","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35127","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52850","marks":["bold"],"text":"E3"},{"id":"spn-52851","text":" unknown / empty / foreign-member splits are typed refusals, and the"}]}],"id":"blk-35126","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35128","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52852","text":"unknown-split error names the splits that do exist."}]},{"id":"blk-35129","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35131","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52853","marks":["bold"],"text":"E4"},{"id":"spn-52854","text":" run order is the sorted task ids regardless of manifest order."}]}],"id":"blk-35130","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35133","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52855","marks":["bold"],"text":"E5"},{"id":"spn-52856","text":" the index invents no identity (id-family scan + forbidden keys)."}]}],"id":"blk-35132","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35135","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52857","marks":["bold"],"text":"E6/E10"},{"id":"spn-52858","text":" one episode per task, distinct ids for distinct tasks, totals are"}]}],"id":"blk-35134","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35136","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52859","text":"real arithmetic over the episodes."}]},{"id":"blk-35137","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35139","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52860","marks":["bold"],"text":"E8"},{"id":"spn-52861","text":" persisted episodes are genuine closed bundles — each re-verified with"}]}],"id":"blk-35138","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35140","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52862","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs verify-episode"},{"id":"spn-52863","text":", no agent — and the index round-trips."}]},{"id":"blk-35141","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35143","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52864","marks":["bold"],"text":"E9"},{"id":"spn-52865","text":" a bad task is recorded and the split continues (2 of 3 still score 1)."}]}],"id":"blk-35142","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35145","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52866","marks":["bold"],"text":"E11"},{"id":"spn-52867","text":" a "},{"id":"spn-52868","marks":["code"],"text":"trvm.world.v1"},{"id":"spn-52869","text":" package is refused "},{"id":"spn-52870","marks":["italic"],"text":"by name"}]}],"id":"blk-35144","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35146","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52871","text":"("},{"id":"spn-52872","marks":["code"],"text":"SUBSTRATE_NOT_EVALUABLE"},{"id":"spn-52873","text":"), not half-run."}]},{"id":"blk-35147","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35149","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52874","marks":["bold"],"text":"E13"},{"id":"spn-52875","text":" two runs of one split agree exactly ("},{"id":"spn-52876","marks":["code"],"text":"a == b"},{"id":"spn-52877","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-35148","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35151","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52878","text":"CLI: exit 0 all-ok · exit 1 ran-and-disagreed ("},{"id":"spn-52879","marks":["code"],"text":"ok 2/3"},{"id":"spn-52880","text":") · exit 2 unknown"}]}],"id":"blk-35150","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35152","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52881","text":"split / missing package · "},{"id":"spn-52882","marks":["code"],"text":"--json"},{"id":"spn-52883","text":" emits the index."}]},{"id":"blk-35153","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52884","text":"Regression: "},{"id":"spn-52885","marks":["bold"],"text":"314 tests green, 0 failures, 0 skips"},{"id":"spn-52886","text":" — admission 16, cli_evalone 18, cli 12, episode_evidence 56, evalone 14, "},{"id":"spn-52887","marks":["bold"],"text":"eval_split 15"},{"id":"spn-52888","text":", execfacts 8, forge_adapter 6, identity 25, pack 18, patchapply 10, paths 10, real_residency 9, reward 17, runner 10, scaffold 16, snapshot 10, substrate_verifiers 24, vcontext 5, verifiers 15."}]},{"id":"blk-35154","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52889","text":"6. Autonomous decisions — flagged for GPT-5.6"}]},{"id":"blk-35155","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35157","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52890","marks":["bold"],"text":"`eval` mints no artifact id."},{"id":"spn-52891","text":" The index is "},{"id":"spn-52892","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.evaluation.v1"},{"id":"spn-52893","text":" and is"}]}],"id":"blk-35156","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-35158","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52894","text":"not content-addressed. If you want a run over a split to "},{"id":"spn-52895","marks":["italic"],"text":"be"},{"id":"spn-52896","text":" an artifact, it needs an agent identity rung first — otherwise the id closes over less than the thing it names. I did not invent either. "},{"id":"spn-52897","marks":["bold"],"text":"Confirm, or rule the agent rung."}]},{"id":"blk-35159","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35161","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52898","marks":["bold"],"text":"Splits are canonicalized as sorted sets, and this changes `env-…`"},{"id":"spn-52899","text":" for any"}]}],"id":"blk-35160","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-35162","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52900","text":"environment whose split members were not already in sorted order. It is the literal reading of §3 (\"named sets\"), and it makes reordering non-identity — but it "},{"id":"spn-52901","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-52902","text":" a behaviour change to a shipped command. Confirm."}]},{"id":"blk-35163","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35165","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52903","marks":["bold"],"text":"`SPLIT_DUPLICATE` refuses rather than collapses"},{"id":"spn-52904","text":" a repeated member,"}]}],"id":"blk-35164","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-35166","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52905","text":"matching the "},{"id":"spn-52906","marks":["code"],"text":"RemoveObject"},{"id":"spn-52907","text":"/no-auto-repair discipline."}]},{"id":"blk-35167","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35169","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52908","marks":["bold"],"text":"Verifier wiring moved out of the CLI"},{"id":"spn-52909","text":" into "},{"id":"spn-52910","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/wiring.py"},{"id":"spn-52911","text":". It was"}]}],"id":"blk-35168","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-35170","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52912","text":"CLI-private, so a library caller got "},{"id":"spn-52913","marks":["italic"],"text":"zero"},{"id":"spn-52914","text":" verifiers and every episode came back invalid-config. A task's verifier set must be a function of the task, not of the caller, or two runs of one task are not comparable. This was a real defect found by the E6 law, not a refactor for taste."}]},{"id":"blk-35171","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35173","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52915","marks":["bold"],"text":"A low reward is not a disagreement."},{"id":"spn-52916","text":" Exit 1 fires only on "},{"id":"spn-52917","marks":["code"],"text":"invalid"},{"id":"spn-52918","text":" /"}]}],"id":"blk-35172","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-35174","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52919","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-52920","text":" episodes; an agent that legitimately scores 0.25 exits 0. "},{"id":"spn-52921","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-52922","text":" scores, it does not judge."}]},{"id":"blk-35175","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52923","marks":["bold"],"text":"One subject per environment"},{"id":"spn-52924","text":", admitted once and shared by every task in"}]}],"id":"blk-35176","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":6},{"id":"blk-35178","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52925","text":"the split. That is the shape "},{"id":"spn-52926","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-52927","text":" emits today. Per-task subjects would need a different manifest, not a different runner."}]},{"id":"blk-35179","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52928","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trvm.world.v1` is refused by name."},{"id":"spn-52929","text":" It packs and reopens fine, but the"}]}],"id":"blk-35180","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":7},{"id":"blk-35182","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52930","text":"Episode Kernel over a world subject (D5) is unbuilt, so it is a typed refusal rather than a partial run."}]},{"id":"blk-35183","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-52931","text":"7. Not built"}]},{"id":"blk-35184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52932","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs serve --ors/--mcp"},{"id":"spn-52933","text":" (needs the D5 process model), "},{"id":"spn-52934","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-52935","text":" (the outer content-addressed package from D3), and the REPL. With "},{"id":"spn-52936","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-52937","text":" shipped, "},{"id":"spn-52938","marks":["bold"],"text":"§7's build order is exhausted"},{"id":"spn-52939","text":" — everything remaining was explicitly deferred by ruling, so this is a natural halt point."}]},{"id":"blk-35185","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-52940","text":"MIT licensed · TRAAVIIS Holdings · part of the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera2hdq72twwazrafbgc7fz5dn6g6qpvpsqi4m2iv542zhd5v2qxx4q","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}